From 758a73a5c7776d3609dc4bf5acbc495410484fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:39:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Present the owner note as a notice, and stop blocking the
 render on fonts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The note area is now read-only and attributed. Reviews are opinions from
visitors and look like it — grey card, accent bar, stars. An owner note is
different in kind: it is the venue telling people its hours, so it gets a
bordered panel with an "MUASSASA EGASIDAN" header strip and no rating
furniture. The suggest-an-edit pencil is gone from it, matching the social
links: once a value is approved it is fixed, and corrections come to the
admin rather than through the queue.

Tapping a Telegram link no longer closes the Mini App. close() tears the
session down and drops the user back at the start, which is not what
"show me the group" should cost.

Load time: the card was waiting on the Google Fonts stylesheet. A
stylesheet in the head blocks the scripts below it, so the API call did not
even start until the font server answered — 13s in a network where that
host stalls. It is now fetched non-render-blocking (display=swap already
covered the FOUT) and the page scripts are deferred, so they download in
parallel with execution order preserved. Photo probing was the other
serial cost: it now fires a batch of indices and extensions at once, still
stopping at the first gap, and the card renders behind a skeleton instead
of waiting for it.

